From 78d89f68bc3e8ea6c0e4df3f4606dc5ebdfa8bd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mojyack <mojyack@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 08:24:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] avcodec/vp8: reinitialise the hwaccel on a mid-stream
 resolution change

update_dimensions() computes dim_reset, its "the dimensions changed"
flag, from s->macroblocks_base - after vp8_decode_flush_impl(avctx, 1)
has freed exactly that pointer.  So dim_reset is always 0, the
get_pixel_format()/ff_get_format() call below is reached only on the
first frame, and no hwaccel is ever told the size changed.  Frame
threading hides it a second time: each thread starts with
macroblocks_base == NULL, so even with the order corrected only a
single-threaded decode would see it.

The enclosing if is already the test, so set the flag inside it.

Broken since eb6bb8f32fdc ("libavcodec/vp8dec: fix the multi-thread
HWAccel decode error"), which added the flag.

A hwaccel keeps decoding at the negotiated size: a stateless V4L2
decoder refuses the frame outright ("frame dimensions do not match the
negotiated coded format"), and the VP8-TEST-VECTORS streams
vp80-03-segmentation-1425 and -1436 fail on it.  Both are byte-exact
against software with this, taking that suite to 61 of 61 on a Tegra X1.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
 libavcodec/vp8.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vp8.c b/libavcodec/vp8.c
index 40564ec9f9..09aacf20e8 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vp8.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vp8.c
@@ -205,13 +205,13 @@ int update_dimensions(VP8Context *s, int width, int height, int is_vp7)
 
     if (width  != s->avctx->width || ((width+15)/16 != s->mb_width || (height+15)/16 != s->mb_height) && s->macroblocks_base ||
         height != s->avctx->height) {
+        dim_reset = 1;
+
         vp8_decode_flush_impl(s->avctx, 1);
 
         ret = ff_set_dimensions(s->avctx, width, height);
         if (ret < 0)
             return ret;
-
-        dim_reset = (s->macroblocks_base != NULL);
     }
 
     if ((s->pix_fmt == AV_PIX_FMT_NONE || dim_reset) &&
-- 
